# ============================================================
# CODEFEST AD ASTRA 2026 — .gitignore
#
# The submission is a PUBLIC REPO LINK (FAQ: "Se envía enlace a repo
# público a través del form"), so what is here is what the judges see.
# Two rules: never commit the corpus (it is ADL's, 3.14 GB), and never
# commit anything a rebuild regenerates.
# ============================================================

# --- ADL's corpus. Not ours to redistribute, and 3.14 GB.
CORPUS CODEFEST AD ASTRA 2026/
*.xlsx.bak
Indice_Datos_Codefest.xlsx
/entrega/base_vectorial/

# --- Extraction cache. Regenerated by build_index.py; keyed on
#     CHUNKER_VERSION, so a stale copy is worse than none.
.cache_extract/
*.cache/

# --- Environments and interpreter state
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# uv.lock is TRACKED, not ignored. 1.4 asks for a reproducible pipeline, and
# a lockfile is what pins the exact resolved versions for the jury -- the
# whole class of failure this project hit (a resolve silently swapping
# torch's CUDA wheels) is what committing this file prevents for whoever
# clones the repo next. .python-version stays tracked for the same reason.

constraints.txt

# --- Build artefacts and run logs
slow_files.txt
build*.log
*.bak
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.DS_Store

# ============================================================
# entrega/ — the deliverable. TRACK the code, IGNORE the weights.
#
# index.faiss is ~594 MB per encoder: over GitHub's 100 MB hard limit
# per file, so a push fails outright rather than degrading. metadata.jsonl
# is ~400 MB. Both are regenerated by build_index.py from the corpus, so
# the repo stays reproducible without them -- which is exactly what 1.4
# asks for. Deliver them by the channel the organisers specify.
# ============================================================
entrega/base_vectorial/*/index.faiss
entrega/base_vectorial/*/metadata.jsonl
entrega/base_vectorial/*/metadata.jsonl.bak

# Keep: entrega/generador.py, consultas_50.jsonl, resultados.jsonl,
#       informe_tecnico.pdf, encoder.json, and the graph (a few MB, and
#       it is the bonus component -- judges should see it).
!entrega/base_vectorial/*/encoder.json
!entrega/base_vectorial/grafo/grafo.graphml

# --- Local evaluation working files. Keep pool.xlsx and the decision
#     reports: they are the evidence behind the informe's claims.
!pool.xlsx
!docling_decision.json
!docling_files.txt
!triage.json
!inventory.json